I generally find it's sufficient to never let them into the level
I'm currently solving. Leave them by the stairs, go up into level 1,
solve level 1, go down and get them. Then leave them on level 1
while solving level 2, and bring them up to help you out with the
roomful of stuff at the end.

This technique generally seems to keep them tame, out of the way,
and yet still have them around when I need them most.

(Even better is if you have a magic whistle, but there's no
guarantee of having found one in time.)

That said, pets aren't always an advantage: I suffered a
particularly YASD a couple of days ago in which I pushed my pet into
the zoo at the top of Sokoban and let it munch away on things
without me for a bit. As I was nail-bitingly watching it dance
around a mumak in my telepathic vision, a giant bat snuck up and
started nibbling on me, which I completely failed to notice because
the pet/mumak situation was so engrossing. So I just kept on hitting
`.' until I died.

